{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Behold, all of them.</b> Concerning the idols." "Some say that the vav of <b>און</b> is in place of a yod, for the letters yod, heh, vav, alef interchange. And it is possible that it is as it sounds: they are emptiness, and moreover their deeds." "<b>Their molten images.</b> Some say [it is] from the root of עגל מסכה (Exodus 32:4). But the correct [interpretation] in my eyes: the nesikhim are what their worshippers pour out for them."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:29.566583521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}